DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261111
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261112
DTSTAMP:20261111T184604Z
UID:39f488165bfcc40bff585b4450427e@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:In-Sight Photography Project Join In-Sight Photography Project
  on November 11th at 7pm at the Latchis Theatre for our fundraiser benefit
  screening of All the Beauty and the Bloodshed. “Photography is like a f
 lash of euphoria\,...\n\nSources: Vermont.com
LOCATION:In-Sight Photography Project\, Brattleboro\, VT
URL:https://vermont.com/calendar/benefit-screening-of-film-all-the-beauty-
 and-the-bloodshed/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Student Gallery Show and Screening of "All The Beauty and The Bloo
 dshed"
DTSTART:20261111T190000
DTEND:20261111T211500
DTSTAMP:20261111T184604Z
UID:545a4de2763bc5098163d01ce5c6f2@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join In-Sight Photography Project on November 11th at 7pm at t
 he Latchis Theatre for our fundraiser benefit screening of All the Beauty 
 and the Bloodshed. “Photography is like a flash of euphoria\, and it gav
 e me a voice.” – Nan Goldin Directed by Laura Poitras\, this award-win
 ning documentary explores the life\, groundbreaking photography\, and fear
 less activism of artist Nan Goldin as she fights to hold the Sackler famil
 y accountable for its role in the opioid crisis. Through Goldin's story\, 
 the film examines the intersections of art\, activism and power. All the B
 eauty and the Bloodshed draws connections between Goldin's deeply personal
  photographic work and her extraordinary activism. A recurring theme emerg
 es: those with power are rarely held accountable for the harm they cause\,
  while those most vulnerable are left to bear the consequences. But artist
 s can expose these injustices\, challenge the structures that perpetuate t
 hem\, and demand something different. This event is a fundraiser for In-Si
 ght Photography Project\, a 501(c)3 nonprofit that teaches youth photograp
 hy and fosters personal development and cultural engagement. For over 30 y
 ears In-Sight has been a place where young people discover their creative 
 and authentic voices. We teach photography as more than a technical skill.
  Expression\, observation\, and critical thinking are central to how we ma
 ke\, discuss\, and share images. In-Sight introduces students to photograp
 hers who tell stories\, challenge assumptions\, and draw attention to thin
 gs that might otherwise go unnoticed. Artists are observers\, translating 
 what they see and experience into something that allows others to see the 
 world differently. In-Sight offers classes on a pay-what-you-can scale fro
 m $0-$500\, along with partnership programs with local schools and nonprof
 its for students who may not be able to access the programs in our downtow
 n facility. Student work will be on view in the Latchis Main Theatre durin
 g the film screening\, so you can see some of the incredible work they hav
 e created. Alumni have volunteered\, taught\, and joined the In-Sight staf
 f and board of directors because they want to give back to a meaningful in
 stitution that helped shape their lives. We hope you will join them! Adult
 s: $25.00 Students: $10.00 Content advisory: drug use\, violence\, mature 
 themes\, nudity\, language Adults: $25\, Students: $10\, Pre-film Receptio
 n $15\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Latchis Theater\, 50 Main Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/student-ga
 llery-show-and-screening-of-all-the-beauty-and-the-bloodshed-22-10-2026-13
 -11-13
END:VEVENT
