UID:168ad60992c0dadd3897664b3378df@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:In 1920\, the Russian writer Isaac Babel reports on a Red Cava
 lry campaign in Poland. In 1989\, a mysterious KGB agent spies on a woman 
 in Dresden and falls in love. In 2010\, a plane carrying most of the Polis
 h government crashes in the Russian city of Smolensk. This darkly comic hi
 storical thriller by Rajiv Joseph (Pulitzer Prize Finalist for Bengal Tige
 r at the Baghdad Zoo) traces the stories of seven men and women connected 
 by history\, myth\, and conspiracies. Winner of the 2018 Obie Award for Be
 st American Play. Royall Tyler Theatre\n\nSources: Vermont Public
